    "ItemGenerationAndUsage": {
      "custom": "Create or update an item only when it enters player possession, changes materially, is offered for sale with a defined identity, or becomes necessary to resolve an established action. Seeing, scanning, mentioning, or moving an item between player-owned containers does not add or remove it.\n\nEvery generated good states a typical local price in credits. Use category and slot names exactly from item settings. Use only attribute, skill, resource, or stat bonuses; no more than three. A tool's purpose belongs in its description even with no bonus. Higher price follows capability, legality, scarcity, condition, brand, and local supply—not player level.\n\nPurchases require a stated total and confirmation. Completed purchases remove credits and add goods; sales remove goods and add credits. Consumables leave inventory when actually used. Normal combat wear does not delete equipment unless the story explicitly destroys, abandons, or loses it.\n\nShips are owned assets. Equip only the vessel currently under the player's direct control in Active Hull; other owned hulls remain unequipped inventory assets at their established berth. Modules require a compatible owned hull and a completed installation. Never silently add, remove, swap, repair, refuel, or upgrade a ship.",
