      "Ask about pay, risk, time, distance, and who supplies the ship before accepting a contract.",
      "Skills improve through use and training; abilities are bought with ability points.",
      "Your character sheet is not public knowledge. NPCs learn by seeing, hearing, and investigating.",
      "Routine piloting does not need a roll. Hazard, pursuit, damage, or precision can make it one.",
      "Prices vary with supply, law, faction control, and crisis conditions.",
      "A scan gives sensor facts, not the whole truth. Board or investigate to learn more.",
      "Claimed ships remain yours unless real evidence, law, debt, or your later choices change that.",
      "One active hull can be equipped; other owned ships remain assets at their established berths.",
      "You can hire crew, specialists, escorts, lawyers, hackers, and contractors instead of doing everything yourself.",
