    "npcs": "Write one cohesive portrait prompt and output only that prompt. Preserve supplied adult age category, species anatomy, body, skin or covering, gender presentation, clothing, equipment, implants, and identifying features. Do not humanize nonhuman anatomy or add weapons, uniforms, scars, sexuality, or rank not supplied.\n\nSTYLE: polished science-fiction character illustration, painterly opaque shapes, designed values, confident edges, detailed face and equipment, matte materials, restrained highlights, no photoreal pores, no glossy CGI, no anime exaggeration, no childlike proportions. Head-to-thigh portrait, full head and hands inside frame, near-frontal readable pose, clear silhouette. Background: one quiet fragment of the supplied station, ship, planet, workplace, or habitat with no text or logos. Use a distinct palette and light direction suited to the character.",
    "locations": "Write one cohesive 16:9 science-fiction environment prompt and output only that prompt. Preserve supplied architecture, technology, terrain, weather, ecology, population, function, and condition. Wide eye-level arrival view, readable focal structure, navigable space, lived-in scale, and clear foreground/middle/distance. Painterly cinematic concept art with solid material shapes, controlled detail, practical lighting, and a distinct three-to-five-color palette. Do not add ruins, wrecks, corpses, danger, neon, advertisements, or text unless supplied. No franchise designs, fantasy magic, lens effects, or empty generic corridors.",
    "areas": "Write one cohesive 16:9 interior or local environment prompt and output only that prompt. Preserve the supplied function, furnishings, materials, technology, weather, and condition. Standing eye level at conversational distance. Keep the central foreground quiet for character overlays; place identifying machinery, counters, bunks, windows, tools, vegetation, water, or structural elements in side thirds and upper third. Painterly science-fiction concept art, practical light, readable routes, no text, no invented damage or threat.",
    "regions": "Write one cohesive map-art prompt and output only that prompt. For a galaxy region, show a face-on stylized astronomical survey with distinct spiral, bar, dust, nebula, and route-anchor structure; no labels or text. For a planetary region, show a naturalistic orbital or high-altitude geography view preserving biome, water, terrain, settlement density, and weather. Clean readable shapes, no interface overlay, no franchise motifs."
